      "content": {
       "id": "v2-e315c9-p7-practice-j1-041921-root",
       "type": "question",
       "label": null,
       "prompt": "The depth of water, $d$ metres, at the end of a jetty in Fremantle is modelled by $d=1.5\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi t}{6}\\right)+4$, where $t$ is the number of hours after 6 am and $0\\leq t\\leq12$.",
       "children": [
        {
         "id": "v2-e315c9-p7-practice-j1-041921-j1-q-a",
         "type": "part",
         "label": "a",
         "prompt": "Show that $\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi t}{6}\\right)=\\frac12$ when the depth is 4.75 metres.",
         "answerSpaceMm": 30,
         "answer": {
          "short": "$\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi t}{6}\\right)=\\frac12$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}4.75&=1.5\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi t}{6}\\right)+4\\\\0.75&=1.5\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi t}{6}\\right)\\\\\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi t}{6}\\right)&=\\frac12\\end{align*}$$"
         }
        },
        {
         "id": "v2-e315c9-p7-practice-j1-041921-j1-q-b",
         "type": "part",
         "label": "b",
         "prompt": "Find the two values of $t$ for which the depth is 4.75 metres.",
         "answerSpaceMm": 50,
         "answer": {
          "short": "$t=1$ and $t=5$.",
          "worked": "Since $0\\leq\\frac{\\pi t}{6}\\leq2\\pi$ and $\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi t}{6}\\right)=\\frac12$,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{\\pi t}{6}&=\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\quad\\text{or}\\quad\\pi-\\frac{\\pi}{6}=\\frac{5\\pi}{6}\\\\t&=1\\quad\\text{or}\\quad t=5.\\end{align*}$$\nThe sine is negative for $\\pi<\\frac{\\pi t}{6}\\leq2\\pi$, so there are no other solutions."
         }
        },
        {
         "id": "v2-e315c9-p7-practice-j1-041921-j1-q-c",
         "type": "part",
         "label": "c",
         "prompt": "At what clock times is the depth 4.75 metres?",
         "answerSpaceMm": 22,
         "answer": {
          "short": "7 am and 11 am.",
          "worked": "$t=1$ is 1 hour after 6 am, which is 7 am.\n\n$t=5$ is 5 hours after 6 am, which is 11 am."
         }
        }
       ],
