       "title": "",
       "content": {
        "id": "v2-proposal-j2-041921-root",
        "type": "question",
        "label": null,
        "prompt": "The depth of water, $d$ metres, in a bay is modelled by $d=k\\cos(at)+c$, where $t$ is the number of hours after midnight. In each case, find the values of $k$, $a$ and $c$.",
        "children": [
         {
          "id": "v2-proposal-j2-041921-j2-gp-a",
          "type": "part",
          "label": "a",
          "prompt": "High tide of 2.9 metres occurs at 5 am and the next low tide of 0.5 metres occurs at 10 am.",
          "answerSpaceMm": 50,
          "answer": {
           "short": "$k=-1.2$, $a=\\frac{\\pi}{5}$, $c=1.7$.",
           "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Amplitude}&=\\frac{2.9-0.5}{2}=1.2\\\\c&=\\frac{2.9+0.5}{2}=1.7\\\\\\text{Period}&=2\\times5=10\\\\a&=\\frac{2\\pi}{10}=\\frac{\\pi}{5}\\end{align*}$$\nAt $t=5$, $\\cos\\pi=-1$, but the depth is a maximum, so $k=-1.2$.\n\nCheck: $d(5)=-1.2(-1)+1.7=2.9$."
          }
         },
         {
          "id": "v2-proposal-j2-041921-j2-gp-b",
          "type": "part",
          "label": "b",
          "prompt": "Low tide of 1.1 metres occurs at 3 am and the next high tide of 3.5 metres occurs at 6 am.",
          "answerSpaceMm": 50,
          "answer": {
           "short": "$k=1.2$, $a=\\frac{\\pi}{3}$, $c=2.3$.",
           "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Amplitude}&=\\frac{3.5-1.1}{2}=1.2\\\\c&=\\frac{3.5+1.1}{2}=2.3\\\\\\text{Period}&=2\\times3=6\\\\a&=\\frac{2\\pi}{6}=\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\end{align*}$$\nAt $t=3$, $\\cos\\pi=-1$ and the depth is a minimum, so $k=1.2$.\n\nCheck: $d(3)=1.2(-1)+2.3=1.1$."
          }
         },
         {
          "id": "v2-proposal-j2-041921-j2-gp-c",
          "type": "part",
          "label": "c",
          "prompt": "High tide of 4.6 metres occurs at 7 am, and the low tide is 1.8 metres. There are 14 hours between successive high tides.",
          "answerSpaceMm": 50,
          "answer": {
           "short": "$k=-1.4$, $a=\\frac{\\pi}{7}$, $c=3.2$.",
           "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Amplitude}&=\\frac{4.6-1.8}{2}=1.4\\\\c&=\\frac{4.6+1.8}{2}=3.2\\\\\\text{Period}&=14\\\\a&=\\frac{2\\pi}{14}=\\frac{\\pi}{7}\\end{align*}$$\nAt $t=7$, $\\cos\\pi=-1$, but the depth is a maximum, so $k=-1.4$.\n\nCheck: $d(7)=-1.4(-1)+3.2=4.6$."
          }
         }
        ]
       },
